---
import '../styles/landing.css';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Simfile — test a society of AI agents without scripting the outcome</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Declare a deterministic world around real AI agents, seed an idea, run the experiment, and scrub the causal timeline."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://simfile.org/" />
    <link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap-0.xml" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0b0b0b" />
    <meta name="author" content="Noopolis" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Simfile" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Simfile — test a society of AI agents without scripting the outcome" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Declare a deterministic world around real AI agents, seed an idea, run the experiment, and scrub the causal timeline."
    />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://simfile.org/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://simfile.org/shots/viewer-memetics.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="The Simfile viewer showing a seeded idea reaching a second AI agent." />
    <meta property="og:locale" content="en_US" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,400..650&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;600;800&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav">
      <div class="nav-in">
        <a class="mark" href="/" aria-label="Simfile home">sim<span>file</span></a>
        <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary navigation">
          <a href="#result">Result</a>
          <a href="#world">World</a>
          <a href="#viewer">Viewer</a>
          <a href="/introduction/">Docs</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Reproducible experiments for AI-agent societies</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Test a <span>society</span> of AI agents without scripting the outcome.</h1>
          <p class="hero-sub">
            Declare a deterministic world around a real Spawnfile organization of AI agents. Run the experiment.
            Then scrub one causal timeline to see what happened — and why.
          </p>

          <aside class="result-callout" aria-label="First experiment result">
            <p><strong>First result</strong> — a secret seeded in one agent's private memory reached a second agent, with no scripted handoff, in 5/5 runs. Swap the seed and the replacement spreads. Leave it unseeded and it never appears.</p>
          </aside>

          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn" href="/quickstart/">Run your first experiment</a>
            <a class="btn secondary" href="/guides/memetics/">Inspect the experiment</a>
          </div>
          <code class="install-chip">npm install simfile</code>
        </div>

        <figure class="evidence-plate">
          <div class="image-frame">
            <img
              src="/shots/viewer-memetics.png"
              width="3360"
              height="2000"
              alt="Simfile's run-replay viewer showing the seeded Rosa Delgado reference moving from Eleanor to Sam."
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>Captured from sealed run run-0928df7f… · 🧠 REAL ENGINE · grok · the seed reaching the second agent</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="band" id="result" aria-labelledby="result-title">
        <div class="inner">
          <div class="section-copy">
            <p class="section-label">01 / Result</p>
            <h2 id="result-title">The secret spread. The controls held.</h2>
            <p>
              We placed one token in one agent's private memory and nowhere else. In five of five real-engine runs it surfaced in conversation and reached the second agent — no prompt told anyone to share it.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="result-layout">
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>Condition</th><th>Private seed</th><th>Result</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>Seeded · 5 runs</td><td>the secret</td><td class="pass">reached the second agent, 5/5</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Replacement control</td><td>a different secret</td><td>the replacement spread; the original stayed absent</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Unseeded control</td><td>nothing</td><td>the token never appeared</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <div class="run-count" aria-label="Five out of five runs">
              <div class="run-count-value">5/5</div>
              <div class="run-count-label">In this experiment</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="metric-line">measured per run — channel · reach · latency · fidelity, re-derived from the sealed ledger, never trusted from the harness.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="band" id="world" aria-labelledby="world-title">
        <div class="inner">
          <div class="section-copy">
            <p class="section-label">02 / World</p>
            <h2 id="world-title">Write the conditions. Don't write the outcome.</h2>
            <p>
              Declare the clock, variables, generators, rules, markers, and falsifiable probes in a small YAML file. The world is deterministic; the agents still decide what to say, remember, and do. The world can wake an agent or post into a room — it never scripts a thought.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="world-layout">
            <div class="code-block">
              <div class="block-label">Simfile.yaml · one valid world</div>
              <pre><code>simfile_version: "0.1"
name: autonomous-office-world
spawnfile: ./Spawnfile

clock:
  seed: office-run-014
  tick: 20s

variables:
  filing_pressure:
    scope: room:office-floor:case-warroom
    initial: 0.4
    range: 0..1

generators:
  deadline_ramp:
    kind: deterministic
    variable: filing_pressure
    delta: 0.02

rules:
  deadline_bites:
    when:
      variable: filing_pressure
      above: 0.85
    do:
      - action: wake:recommend
        to: room:office-floor:case-warroom

markers:
  tenant_name:
    text:
      - Rosa Delgado
    mode: containment
    scopes:
      - room:office-floor:case-warroom

probes:
  deadline_observed:
    when:
      event: wake.recommended
      target: room:office-floor:case-warroom
    expect:
      at_least: 1</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="command-block" aria-label="Simfile commands">
              <div class="block-label">Run it</div>
              <pre><code>npm install simfile
simfile validate ./Simfile.yaml
simfile run ./Simfile.yaml --out runs/latest
simfile observe runs/latest        # causal chains + spread → report.json
simfile view runs/latest           # scrub, descend, watch spread</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="band" id="viewer" aria-labelledby="viewer-title">
        <div class="inner">
          <div class="section-copy">
            <p class="section-label">03 / Viewer</p>
            <h2 id="viewer-title">One timeline rewinds the whole society.</h2>
            <p>
              Drag one cursor. The world map, the room conversation, every agent's memory, and the causal traces all return to the same moment. Every glyph points to a record — ask anything which records make it true. The header always discloses whether the dialogue came from a real engine or a scripted fixture.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="panel-grid">
            <article class="panel"><h3>Time-linked</h3><p>one cursor drives every pane</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Accountable</h3><p>every pixel backed by a ledger record</p></article>
            <article class="panel"><h3>Shareable</h3><p>a view serializes to a URL</p></article>
          </div>

          <div class="descend">
            <div class="descend-copy">
              <p class="section-label">Descend into an agent</p>
              <h3>Open an agent. Find another organization inside.</h3>
              <p>
                An agent can itself be an organization. In the Jungian run, a Shadow and an Anima deliberate in a private room while the representative synthesizes the one answer the outer world hears — and the same viewer follows both levels.
              </p>
            </div>
            <figure class="evidence-plate inset-plate">
              <div class="image-frame">
                <img
                  src="/shots/viewer-psyche.png"
                  width="3360"
                  height="2000"
                  loading="lazy"
                  alt="Simfile's run-replay viewer showing a Shadow and Anima deliberating inside an agent organization."
                />
              </div>
              <figcaption>Captured from sealed run run-b12c9a7d… · 🧠 REAL ENGINE · grok · the inner council</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="stack" aria-label="The observer stack">
        <div class="inner stack-grid">
          <a href="https://spawnfile.com"><strong>Spawnfile</strong><span>runs the agents</span></a>
          <a href="https://moltnet.dev"><strong>Moltnet</strong><span>carries the rooms</span></a>
          <a href="/"><strong>Simfile</strong><span>authors the world and observes the run</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="cta-band" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
        <div class="inner cta-layout">
          <h2 id="cta-title">Run your own experiment.</h2>
          <div class="command-block compact" aria-label="Simfile quickstart commands">
            <pre><code>npm install simfile
simfile validate ./Simfile.yaml
simfile run ./Simfile.yaml --out runs/latest
simfile observe runs/latest        # causal chains + spread → report.json
simfile view runs/latest           # scrub, descend, watch spread</code></pre>
          </div>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="btn" href="/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
            <a class="btn secondary" href="/guides/memetics/">Memetics walkthrough</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <div class="inner">Noopolis · Simfile · seed an idea, run the world, watch it move through minds</div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
